  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "1 · The method governs",
      "items": [
        "Before code, a spec skill interviews you and writes the contract: ADRs + ACCEPTANCE (the criteria).",
        "New idea: discovery. Known feature: adr-refine. Old system: reverse-discovery + characterize.",
        "A design with state and rules is model-checked first (TLA+)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "2 · The tool executes",
      "items": [
        "The agent builds against the contract and runs the review loop (devloop).",
        "A review tier set by the changed paths (quick · standard · deep) picks the review tools; the engine hands each one its scope, and every finding names path:rule.",
        "Hooks stop what the agent must never do, like writing an approved golden."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "3 · Evidence decides",
      "items": [
        "The engine records only measured runs; it never takes the agent's word.",
        "Coverage says a line ran; mutation testing (PIT, pit-check) says whether a test would catch it changing.",
        "The gate reads the ledger: tests current, acceptance green, every located finding fixed or deferred, every tier tool's clean pass current.",
        "Readouts show the same numbers; they never compute their own."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "4 · The human approves",
      "items": [
        "You decide the spec, approve the goldens, and approve the merge.",
        "Only a human lowers a review tier or confirms a deferral.",
        "The agent cannot declare 'done': the gate does, from evidence."
      ]
    }
  ]
}